    <statement><p>Let <m>f(x,y)=x^{2}y^{3}</m> and <m>c(t)=\left(2t^{2},t^{3}\right)</m></p>
<p>(a) Calculate:</p>
<p><m>\nabla f \cdot c'(t)=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) Use the Chain Rule for Paths to evaluate <m>\frac{d}{dt}f(c(t))</m> at <m>t=1</m>.</p>
<p><m>\frac{d}{dt}f(c(1))=</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>8xy^{3}t+9x^{2}y^{2}t^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>52</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f(x,y)=x^{2}y^{3}</m>
<me>\frac{\partial{f}}{\partial{x}}=2xy^{3}, \quad \frac{\partial{f}}{\partial{y}}=3x^{2}y^{2}</me>
The gradient vector is thus
<me>\nabla f=\left\lt 2xy^{3},3x^{2}y^{2}\right&gt;</me>
Also,
<me>c'(t)=\left\lt  \left(cx\right)', \left(cy\right)' \right&gt;=\left\lt 4t, 3t^{2}\right&gt;</me>
<me>\nabla f \cdot c'(t)=\left\lt 2xy^{3},3x^{2}y^{2}\right&gt;\cdot\left\lt 4t, 3t^{2}\right&gt;=8xy^{3}t+9x^{2}y^{2}t^{2}</me>



(b) Using the Chain Rule and substituting <m>x=2t^{2}, y=t^{3}</m> gives
<me>\frac{d}{dt}f(c(t))=\frac{d}{dt}\left(4t^{4}t^{9}\right)=\frac{d}{dt}\left(4t^{13}\right)=52t^{12}</me>
At the point <m>t=1</m>, we obtain
<me>\left.\frac{d}{dt}f(c(t))\right|_{t=1}=\left.52t^{12}\right|_{t=1}=52</me>





</solution>
